course: dictionary
lesson: 13544
title: Impractical: not sensible in real life
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Impractical means not sensible or useful in real life, or hard to use. Look at its parts: im- means not, and practical means useful or sensible, so impractical means not practical. «Wearing flip-flops to climb a muddy hill is impractical.» Flip-flops slip off and do not protect your feet, so the clues show they are a bad choice for that job.
explain: The word can also describe a person. «Dad is impractical; he can never fix a loose bike chain.» Here impractical means he is not good at everyday practical tasks. It can also describe a plan with unrealistic ideas, such as «Her plan to carry twenty balloons up the stairs was impractical.»
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «not sensible» in place of impractical: «Wearing flip-flops to climb a muddy hill is not sensible.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: «Impractical» means not sensible or useful in real life, or hard to use.
fact: «Impractical» can also describe a person who is not good at everyday practical tasks, or who has unrealistic ideas.
fact: The noun is «impracticality», and the opposite of «impractical» is «practical».
fact: In design technology, you test whether a design is practical or impractical to use.
fact: Phrases you may meet: «totally impractical», «impractical for» a job, and «an impractical idea».
exercise: «The tiny umbrella kept only one raindrop off her head, so it was totally impractical.» What does impractical mean here? | Very large and heavy | Very colourful and bright | *Not useful or sensible in real life | Made of wood
exercise: Which word is the opposite of impractical? | *practical | impossible | important | impolite
exercise: «Ella's chair design had no seat, so it was impractical.» What is the clue that shows it is impractical? | It was painted blue | Ella drew it on paper | It had four legs | *You could not sit on it
test: «Mia packed a glass vase to take on a camping trip, which was impractical.» What is the best reason? | It is very pretty | It is made of glass, so it is clear | Camping is fun | *It could break easily and is not sensible for camping
test: Lee says, «Dad's idea to fly to school with a kite is totally impractical.» What does impractical mean? | Very fast and quick | Very loud and noisy | *Not sensible or useful in real life | Full of joy
exam: Which word best describes a person who cannot fix a leaking tap or build a shelf? | Curt | Luminous | *Impractical | Ancient
